ighly malleable depending on  environment and then last but definitely  not least as an extremely important crux  in all of this if you're dealing with  something biological like genetic IQ you  have to be weighing it against something  that is also biological it would be  totally meaningless for example for us  to do research on the correlation  between having red hair and being a  libertarian one is a biological trait  one is a socially constructed trait race  is a socially constructed trait not a  distinct biological concept  but this is the position of the NIH the  APA the American Anthropological  Association there is no gene or set of  genes that all people from one race have  there's so much genetic diversity within  what we refer to as races that any  conversation about weighing a biological  variable like genetic IQ against race is  moot from the beginning but some people  were even saying that the NIH and the  APA take this position on race because  they are institutions controlled by  liberals I do want to just break this  down again because it really is what  makes the entire race realist argument  about genetic IQ completely implode in  biology we do not have genetically  discrete groups based on continent of  origin or skin color or what we would  call black white asian Indian Hispanic  we have patterns of continuous variation  from a continental level all the way  down to the population level rather than  these abrupt clear differences between  continents this is an example we used in  the other video but I think it's a good  one  sickle cell anemia there's a  misconception that black people get this  disease because there's something  genetically that black people have in  common  here's a map of the distribution of  sickle-cell anemia which is common in  the Middle East and India as well  because it develops where malaria is  common it has nothing to do with being  black or african and black people  sharing DNA there's nothing that all  Africans or Asians or white people have  in common within their races that's not  shared between races but you might be  thinking people within races have to  share something genetically because I  can look at someone and I can tell what  race they are there are physical  features in common and these are based  on genes like for example these two  people clearly these are two people of  African descent there's something  visually distinct about people of  African descent you'd be wrong the man  on the left is an Aboriginal Australian  and the boy on the right is a Jarawa and  indigenous people of the Andaman Islands  in Southeast Asia we  nothing about their genetics by looking  at them and your average person from  either of these two regions would have  very little in common genetically with  someone from Africa dark skin dark kinky  hair is an adaptive trait that developed  some people who live near the equator on  any continent and by the same token a  person from Nigeria and a person from  Zimbabwe wouldn't be assumed to  necessarily have much in common  genetically either neither would someone  from France and someone from Russia even  though they may both look white so you  quickly realize why trying to correlate  a specific genetic trait with a  genetically arbitrary variable like race  or continent doesn't get you anywhere  you have to under the understand the  difference here between the general  notion of IQ being heritable on an  individual basis from parent to child  which is all that we actually learn from  the twin studies where we see IQ  inherited to some degree and the more  specific notion that there's evidence  for average genetic IQ differences  between races which would then also  assume that race is even a valid factor  biologically against which to measure  genetic IQ differences it's time to move  on from this it's passe I know I will  get another series of rebuttals from  people in the audience but for the time  being we've said more than enough about  race and IQ and there are really  important issues that we actually have  to solve on planet Earth for Homo  sapiens future
 

